notes.body:
It will probably be a magic number for most use cases. For a lot of the easy cases in IP/TCP/UDP the lookup of the child can be done with the abbreviated field name which is nice when it works. Right now it causes some duplication since I included the field name in the assert_x_field functions, but that is fixable.
```
-    assert_uint_field(get_child_n(udp, 0), "udp.srcport", FT_UINT16, 0x1122);
+    assert_uint_field(get_child(udp, "udp.srcport"), "udp.srcport", FT_UINT16, 0x1122);
```

Right now I'm not sure what to do about fields like "udp.port" that have more than one node with the same name, or most of the stuff in bt-dht that is either unnamed or uses something very generic.

